[ 50.160] CM360_DS218> help fatload
[ 50.163] fatload - load binary file from a dos filesystem
[ 50.165] 
[ 50.165] Usage:
[ 50.171] fatload <interface> [<dev[:part]> [<addr> [<filename> [bytes [pos]]]]]
[ 50.177]     - Load binary file 'filename' from 'dev' on 'interface'
[ 50.180]       to address 'addr' from dos filesystem.
[ 50.185]       'pos' gives the file position to start loading from.
[ 50.191]       If 'pos' is omitted, 0 is used. 'pos' requires 'bytes'.
[ 50.197]       'bytes' gives the size to load. If 'bytes' is 0 or omitted,
[ 50.200]       the load stops on end of file.
[ 50.205]       If either 'pos' or 'bytes' are not aligned to
[ 50.211]       ARCH_DMA_MINALIGN then a misaligned buffer warning will
[ 50.218]       be printed and performance will suffer for the load.
